  "body": "What happens: `camcraft-ui` does not open a file that is given on the command line. The option parser skips a plain argument (`crates/ui/src/cli_options.rs`, `parse`), and the app starts with an empty project. The operating system \"Open with\" and another program that starts CamCraft with a file cannot open a model.\n\nExpected:\n- `camcraft-ui part.stl` (also `.obj`, `.step`, `.stp` and a Solidcraft `.sc`) imports the model through `CommandKind::ImportFile`. This is the same command that a drop and the Model dialog use, so the worker and the update-or-spawn decision stay shared.\n- `camcraft-ui job.camproj` opens the project.\n- A file that CamCraft cannot read, more than one file, or a path that is not a file is refused by name on the status line. The app starts with an empty project. It does not crash.\n- `--help` shows the file argument.\n\nWhy: Solidcraft proposes a \"Send to CamCraft\" command (Solidcraft RFC 0001, phase 1: https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft/blob/main/docs/rfcs/0001-craft-bridge.md). That command starts CamCraft with the design's path. The RFC asks this as open question 2.\n\nOut of scope: a running window that takes the file from a second start (single instance). That is a separate issue.\n\nDone means: a test starts the app state with each file kind and finds the model or project loaded; a test finds the refusals by name; `--help` lists the argument.\n\nSuggested labels (I cannot set labels): `enhancement`, `P6`, `effort:medium`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`.\n",
